              "name": "Mattermost URL",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A URL was found near a 'mattermost' or 'mm_url'/'mm_server'/etc keyword. This is a helper rule used for token validation against the detected Mattermost instance. The 'mm' prefix requires a separator followed by a URL-related keyword to avoid matching unrelated text that happens to start with 'mm' (e.g., tweet content, date formats).\n"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "kingfisher.mattermost.2",
              "name": "Mattermost Access Token",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A Mattermost access token was found near a 'mattermost' or 'mm' keyword. Mattermost tokens are 26-character z-base-32 encoded strings used to authenticate API requests. An attacker could use the token to access the Mattermost instance as the associated user or bot.\n"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://developers.mattermost.com/api-documentation/"
            },
            {
              "id": "kingfisher.mattermost.3",
              "name": "Mattermost Incoming Webhook URL",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A Mattermost incoming webhook URL was found. Webhook URLs allow posting messages to Mattermost channels without further authentication. An attacker could use the webhook URL to post messages, conduct phishing, or exfiltrate data through the channel.\n"
